PREDICT2 -- #530 closing pass 5, Opus measuring seat, SECOND batch (the coordinator's panel findings, received mid-run).
Written BEFORE these legs are built or run and before disc530c5b.py has run on any binary (mtime is the order proof).
Mutants: instrument/mut530c5b.py.  Same clone, same baseline, same frozen 185-row probe as batch 1.

LEG      EDIT                                                              PREDICTED  RED ROWS (exact set)
WW6      glm: the write forward DUPLICATED at len 6 only                    185/185    none (a subset of WWtail)
RD2post  codex: a second READ forward AFTER the packing loop (the guest     161/185    rdq r1/r2/r4/r8 (4), stub0-3
         keeps the FIRST read's byte)                                                   r1/r2/r4/r8 (16), tailq r
                                                                                        t7/t6/t5/t3 (4).  GREEN: cmos r*,
                                                                                        iir lca rd, iir lca rd2/rd4/rd8 --
                                                                                        so at LANES 1 and 2 the stub rows
                                                                                        are the SOLE carrier of this form
cdxZL3   codex, exact: post-store read iff lane 3 && data[ofs] == 0,        185/185    none (stub3 stores 0x5a; every other
         write result preserved                                                         lane-3 store lands on inert SCR)
Wpure    (disc-only subject for the 8253 channel; no probe leg)             --         --

DISCRIMINATOR disc530c5b.py (8253 counters 0/1/2 = lanes 0/1/2 and the tail port 0x40; stub 0x63/0x61 with a zero store):
  base     live 0x34/0x12 on every counter; PS X -> X/0x12; PL L -> dlv L, r1 0x12; EZ flips 0x0/0x0/0x10.
  Wpure    PS flipped (0x12/X) at lanes 0-2 and every tail, BOTH data values; PL as base.
  WWall    PS flipped at lanes 0-2 and tails; PL as base.
  WWtail   PS flipped at tail6 and tail3 only; direct lanes as base.        WW6: tail6 only.
  dNZtail  PS flipped at tail6 X=0x5a and tail3 X=0x5a only; tail6 X=0 and direct lanes as base.
  RD2post  PL r1 == L at lanes 0-2 and the tails (dlv L); PS as base.
  RD2z     PL L=0 only: dlv 0x12, r1 0x0 (lanes 0-2, tail6); L=0x5a phases as base.
  cdxZL3   all 8253 phases as base (lane 3 has no counter); EZ stub63 zero-store flip 0x10, stub61 as base.
So the 8253 is predicted to catch forms 1 (duplicated store), 2 (RD2post) and 4 (RD2z) at lanes 0-2 and the tail port --
data-independent for the store forms (X = 0 and 0x5a both flip) -- and CANNOT reach lane 3 (0x43 is the control word
port: a read returns mode_byte with no side effect), so form 3 (cdxZL3) stays stub-only.  Its mandatory control is the
`live' pair (two flat reads after a control word return LSB then MSB); a mutant of dev_8253.c that stops the flip-flop
would green every PS/PL row, and `live' is what reds.
